# Proposed features recognized from block_outline.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.
# imported with --allowance 1.0: the blank stands 1.0 above the model's top and outside its plan; bores at the model's top are drilled from the blank top
# or placed by z=, and the plan-bounding rim is proposed as a boss to bring to size

# F2: the level at z=26.0, below the part's topmost height and with nothing beside it rising above it: 1 face (F2) at one height; nothing stands above it outside a proposed feature, so the whole blank clears to it around what stands, the islands and voids derived from containment (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F2_Floor, stepover=...)  [the whole blank down to z=26.0, around what stands higher]
# then finish with: run End(tool=..., surface=F2_Floor, stepover=...)
# what stands higher is an island by containment, and a pocket or bore that opens in this floor is
# cut from it by its own run
feature F2_Floor Plane(z=26.0)

# F9: pocket floor at z=21.0; vertical wall loop F7 F10 F26, mouth at z=26.0, depth 5.0, opens upward; 1 inner wire -- standing material inside the pocket proposes beside it; the floor runs out onto F1, which falls away from it -- that side is open, the loop drawn straight out past the blank; mouth rounded R1.0 (F4 F11 F14) -- proposed as edge_round, the mouth at the round's top (CHECKLIST row 2.1)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F9_Pocket, stepover=...)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# or finish with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F9_Pocket, comp=control)
# comp=control is required on recognized profile Side runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# this floor has 1 inner wire: a boss proposed INSIDE this loop is its island, derived from
# containment -- the Clear above goes around it (stepover at most the tool's radius), and the
# island takes no Clear of its own. CHECK that every inner wire has a proposed boss below:
# standing material this reader could not name is NOT in the proposal, and would be cleared through.
# open toward F1: the floor runs out onto a face that falls away, so
# that side is drawn straight out past the blank, where the engine reads it open;
# everything the loop holds past the floor is air in the model above this floor
# break the mouth with: run Form(tool=<CornerRounder>, surface=F9_Pocket)  [its ground arc must be R1.0]
feature F9_Pocket ProfilePocket(z=26.0, extent=5.0, edge_round=1.0
    -1.02 12.0
    40.0 12.0
    40.0 28.0
    -1.02 28.0
)

# F16: outer profile under top cap F2: vertical wall loop F6 F21 F20 F16, top at z=26.0, base at z=14.0, material inside the loop; stepped base: the profile stops at the highest base z=14.0, and F6 to z=0.0 run on below it; the base at z=14.0 is the head's own underside (the face under the walls faces down): the wall is traced from above, the underside is the other setup's; top edge rounded R1.0 (F12 F13 F15) -- proposed as edge_round, the loop read at the walls; beveled instead where a strip stands (F1: 12.0 deep at 90.0deg included) -- that edge's first point carries chamfer_depth, and 0 on the next goes back to the round; under the head nothing stands outside its outline down to z=10.0, so the wall is proposed down to there, past the underside at z=14.0: outside it is only the blank's side (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F16_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the base is stepped: this profile stops at z=14.0, the highest base; the walls F6 run on below it
# and belong to whatever stands lower -- declare that by hand or accept its own proposal
# the base at z=14.0 is an overhang: the face under the walls faces down, so the
# tool has air under it at the base; the underside itself is the other setup's
# break the top edge with: run Form(tool=<CornerRounder>, surface=F16_Profile)  [its ground arc must be R1.0]
# where the model has a bevel, not a round, the edge's first point carries chamfer_depth and
# the next point's 0 goes back to the round; the angle is the one the model measures --
# cut it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F16_Profile)  [engine comp; a face wider than
# the mill's flank is cut in steps]
# the wall is traced down to z=10.0, past the head's underside at z=14.0: under the
# head nothing stands outside this outline, and the blank's side there is otherwise no setup's
feature F16_Profile ProfileBoss(z=26.0, extent=16.0, edge_round=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0
    0.0 0.0 chamfer_depth=12.0
    0.0 40.0 chamfer_depth=0.0
    60.0 40.0
    60.0 0.0
)

# F27: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material inside (a standing boss), flat top cap F29, clean base at z=21.0 (CHECKLIST row 2.4)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F27_Boss, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# the tool rides outside at R + r_tool (convex flank; finish_cylinder's mirror)
feature F27_Boss CylinderBoss(dia=8.0, extent=9.0, x=32.0, y=20.0, z=21.0)

# F29: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F29_Top Plane(z=30.0)
